   Here, we have wrapped the API call in a try-catch block and thrown an error if the necessary parameter `userId` is not present in the query string. This error will then be caught by the error middleware we defined earlier and handled appropriately.

That's it! With this set up, you can handle errors and ensure your server is more predictable and robust. Remember, error handling is an ongoing process and requires attention in your codebase. Don't hesitate to review your error handling strategies often, and refactor your error handling middleware as necessary.

