   ```bash
   sudo growpart /dev/xvda - /                     
   sudo resize2fs /dev/xvda1 
   ```

7. En tu aplicación Laravel, crea un nuevo archivo en la carpeta `app/Console/Commands` llamado `CreateLaravelDuskUser.php`. Agrega el siguiente contenido para crear un usuario con permisos suficientes para conectarse a AWS:

   ```php
   <?php

   namespace App\Console\Commands;

   use Illuminate\Console\Command;
   use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Artisan;
   use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Hash;

   class CreateLaravelDuskUser extends Command
   {
       /**
        * The name and signature of the console command.
        *
        * @var string
        */
       protected $signature = 'make:dusk-user {--force}';

       /**
        * The console command description.
        *
        * @var string
        */
       protected $description = 'Create a Laravel Dusk user to run tests';

       /**
        * Create a new command instance.
        */
       public function __construct()
       {
           parent::__construct();
       }

       /**
        * Execute the console command.
        *
        * @return mixed
        */
       public function handle()
       {
           $userName = 'dusk';

           $user = \App\User::where('name', $userName)->first();

           if ($this->option('force') || $user === null) {
               $password = Hash::make(secure_random(8));

               $user = new \App\User();
               $user->name = $userName;
               $user->email = 'dusk@yourdomain.com';
               $user->password = $password;

               $user->syncRoles('admin'); // or your desired role

               $user->save();

               Artisan::call('db:seed', [
                   '--class' => 'Spatie\Permission\Eloquent\Seeders\HasRolesSeeder',
               ]);
           } else {
               $this->error('The dusk user already exists.');
           }

           $this->info('The Laravel Dusk user has been created successfully.');

           $this->line("Username: {$userName}");
           $this->line("Password: {$password}");
       }
   }
   ```

8. Ejecuta el comando `php artisan make:dusk-user --force` para crear un nuevo usuario con los permisos adecuados.

